// A small bakery's sales over one week, compared day by day between the shop counter and online orders.
// The values are sample numbers for showing the shape, not measured figures.
chart A bakery's sales over one week (yen) [shape: line]

item shop as Counter [color: amber]
item online as Online [color: blue]

step Mon
  say The week starts with 42,000 yen at the counter and 12,000 yen online.
  set shop: 42000
  set online: 12000

step Tue
  say On a rainy Tuesday the counter drops to 38,000 yen, and online grows to 15,000 yen.
  set shop: 38000
  set online: 15000

step Wed
  say The counter comes back to 45,000 yen, and online is 14,000 yen.
  set shop: 45000
  set online: 14000

step Thu
  say The counter takes 40,000 yen, and online grows to 18,000 yen.
  set shop: 40000
  set online: 18000

step Fri
  say People on their way home from work lift the counter to 56,000 yen.
  set shop: 56000
  set online: 22000

step Sat
  say The counter has its best day of the week at 78,000 yen.
  set shop: 78000
  set online: 20000

step Sun
  say The counter takes 71,000 yen, and online has its best day at 26,000 yen.
  set shop: 71000
  set online: 26000
